[2026-03-14T22:50:54.192Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VqJXLnYGH7eUKb7ftoVkWS","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\nReplay MCP is a tool for inspecting Replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution data. The documentation outlines three key investigation phases:\n\n**Core Workflow:**\nThe guide recommends: \"Frame your task in the form of a question that you need to answer\" before exploring, then use tools to identify relevant events, understand causation, form hypotheses, and support conclusions with gathered data.\n\n**Tool Categories:**\n\n*Exploratory tools* discover what happened:\n- Error detection (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline analysis (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n- Source inspection (finding and reading code)\n\n*Explanatory tools* reveal why events occurred:\n- Dependency tracking (stack frames, control flow)\n- State details (point inspection, DOM elements, expressions)\n\n**Key Insight:**\n\"The Logpoint tool is extremely useful for this: see the value of the same expression whenever a statement executed, look for anything unexpected, and continue investigating from there.\" This approach helps identify unexpected behavior patterns during execution.\n\nThe system treats recordings as comprehensive execution databases with two fundamental concepts: points (specific execution moments) and elements (persistent DOM references)."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5d795d1b-cd40-4f9d-8a86-66314d0138eb","uuid":"af920d9c-ff14-4243-898c-d2558cb2285e","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\nReplay MCP is a tool for inspecting Replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution data. The documentation outlines three key investigation phases:\n\n**Core Workflow:**\nThe guide recommends: \"Frame your task in the form of a question that you need to answer\" before exploring, then use tools to identify relevant events, understand causation, form hypotheses, and support conclusions with gathered data.\n\n**Tool Categories:**\n\n*Exploratory tools* discover what happened:\n- Error detection (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline analysis (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n- Source inspection (finding and reading code)\n\n*Explanatory tools* reveal why events occurred:\n- Dependency tracking (stack frames, control flow)\n- State details (point inspection, DOM elements, expressions)\n\n**Key Insight:**\n\"The Logpoint tool is extremely useful for this: see the value of the same expression whenever a statement executed, look for anything unexpected, and continue investigating from there.\" This approach helps identify unexpected behavior patterns during execution.\n\nThe system treats recordings as comprehensive execution databases with two fundamental concepts: points (specific execution moments) and elements (persistent DOM references).","durationMs":3355,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-14T22:50:56.784Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RCCLuPGSKUpEh6H3oxMDVb","type":"tool_result","content":"# replay-cli\n\n**Description:** Record your application to gather performance data and debug issues. It enables users to install Replay CLI, record a session, upload and manage them.\n\n**Allowed Tools:** Bash(replayio:*), mcp__replay\n\n## Installation\n\nInstall Replay CLI globally using your preferred package manager:\n\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n# or\nyarn add -g replayio\n# or\npnpm i -g replayio\n# or\nbun i -g replayio\n```\n\n## Authentication\n\nNavigate to https://app.replay.io settings page, create your API key and save it in the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Available Commands\n\n| Command              | Arguments    | Options                                                           |\n| -------------------- | ------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `info`               | –            | –                                                                 |\n| `list`               | –            | `--json`                                                          |\n| `login`              | –            | –                                                                 |\n| `logout`             | –            | –                                                                 |\n| `record`             | `[url]`      | –                                                                 |\n| `remove`             | `[ids...]`   | `-a`, `--all`                                                     |\n| `update`             | –            | –                                                                 |\n| `upload`             | `[ids...]`   | –                                                                 |\n| `upload-source-maps` | `<paths...>` | `-g`, `--group`, `-x`, `--extensions`, `-i`, `--ignore`, `--root` |\n| `help`               | –            | –                                                                 |\n\nPass `-h` or `--help` to any command for more information.\n\n## Command Details\n\n- **`replayio info`** - Shows installed Replay dependencies, CLI version, and Replay Browser info\n- **`replayio list`** - Lists local recordings with ID, host, date, duration, and status; `--json` for detailed output\n- **`replayio login`** - Opens browser to log into your Replay account\n- **`replayio logout`** - Logs out (doesn't invalidate API keys in environment variables)\n- **`replayio record [url]`** - Launches Replay Browser and records the given URL (default: `about:blank`)\n- **`replayio remove [ids...]`** - Removes recordings; use `-a`/`--all` for all recordings\n- **`replayio update`** - Updates Replay Browser only\n- **`replayio upload [ids...]`** - Uploads recordings and returns viewing URL\n- **`replayio upload-source-maps <paths...>`** - Uploads source maps with grouping and filtering options\n- **`replayio help`** - Displays all available commands\n\n## Core Workflow\n\n**Record and upload:**\n```sh\nreplayio record https://myapp.com\n```\n\n**Upload specific recording:**\n```sh\nreplayio upload <recording-id>\n```\n\n**Install MCP Server:**\n```\nclaude --mcp-config \"{\n    \\\"mcpServers\\\": {\n      \\\"replay\\\": {\n        \\\"type\\\": \\\"http\\\",\n        \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://dispatch.replay.io/nut/mcp\\\",\n        \\\"headers\\\": {\n          \\\"Authorization\\\": \\\"${REPLAY_API_KEY}\\\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\"\n```"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5d795d1b-cd40-4f9d-8a86-66314d0138eb","uuid":"751f1e98-6933-4d02-a5b1-33fd1403f3f6","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# replay-cli\n\n**Description:** Record your application to gather performance data and debug issues. It enables users to install Replay CLI, record a session, upload and manage them.\n\n**Allowed Tools:** Bash(replayio:*), mcp__replay\n\n## Installation\n\nInstall Replay CLI globally using your preferred package manager:\n\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n# or\nyarn add -g replayio\n# or\npnpm i -g replayio\n# or\nbun i -g replayio\n```\n\n## Authentication\n\nNavigate to https://app.replay.io settings page, create your API key and save it in the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Available Commands\n\n| Command              | Arguments    | Options                                                           |\n| -------------------- | ------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `info`               | –            | –                                                                 |\n| `list`               | –            | `--json`                                                          |\n| `login`              | –            | –                                                                 |\n| `logout`             | –            | –                                                                 |\n| `record`             | `[url]`      | –                                                                 |\n| `remove`             | `[ids...]`   | `-a`, `--all`                                                     |\n| `update`             | –            | –                                                                 |\n| `upload`             | `[ids...]`   | –                                                                 |\n| `upload-source-maps` | `<paths...>` | `-g`, `--group`, `-x`, `--extensions`, `-i`, `--ignore`, `--root` |\n| `help`               | –            | –                                                                 |\n\nPass `-h` or `--help` to any command for more information.\n\n## Command Details\n\n- **`replayio info`** - Shows installed Replay dependencies, CLI version, and Replay Browser info\n- **`replayio list`** - Lists local recordings with ID, host, date, duration, and status; `--json` for detailed output\n- **`replayio login`** - Opens browser to log into your Replay account\n- **`replayio logout`** - Logs out (doesn't invalidate API keys in environment variables)\n- **`replayio record [url]`** - Launches Replay Browser and records the given URL (default: `about:blank`)\n- **`replayio remove [ids...]`** - Removes recordings; use `-a`/`--all` for all recordings\n- **`replayio update`** - Updates Replay Browser only\n- **`replayio upload [ids...]`** - Uploads recordings and returns viewing URL\n- **`replayio upload-source-maps <paths...>`** - Uploads source maps with grouping and filtering options\n- **`replayio help`** - Displays all available commands\n\n## Core Workflow\n\n**Record and upload:**\n```sh\nreplayio record https://myapp.com\n```\n\n**Upload specific recording:**\n```sh\nreplayio upload <recording-id>\n```\n\n**Install MCP Server:**\n```\nclaude --mcp-config \"{\n    \\\"mcpServers\\\": {\n      \\\"replay\\\": {\n        \\\"type\\\": \\\"http\\\",\n        \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://dispatch.replay.io/nut/mcp\\\",\n        \\\"headers\\\": {\n          \\\"Authorization\\\": \\\"${REPLAY_API_KEY}\\\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\"\n```","durationMs":6263,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
